OL,3,A'It's like a dog set loose on us' -
OL,4,Afear over Kenya's crackdown on foreign
OL,5,Atraders
OL,6,
OL,7,FFor Ndaikech Ali, who has been
OL,8,Ftraversing the streets of the Kenyan
OL,9,Fcapital eking out a living as a tuk-tuk
OL,10,Fdriver for the past nine years,
OL,11,FNairobi's traffic - not xenophobia -
OL,12,Fhas been his biggest concern.
OL,14,FDuring his time in the East African
OL,15,Fnation, the Burundian says he has
OL,16,Falways found Kenyans to be friendly and
OL,17,Fwelcoming - that is until last week,
OL,18,Fwhen the president ordered a crackdown
OL,19,Fon foreigners working as traders or
OL,20,Foperating small-scale businesses.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
